<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Case Study: A <span id="A1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ThinC</span>-4B Trajectory on AIME 2026 Problem 3</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To illustrate the structural pattern of <span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ThinC</span>, we walk through one full rollout on
<span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AIME 2026 Problem 3</span>. The trajectory shows how a single brief
strategic plan in NL transitions into a sequence of code-centric
reasoning steps, each conditioned on the previous interpreter output,
with the final answer emerging from code execution rather than from
NL-level computation.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Problem</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<blockquote id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Find the number of integers less than or equal to <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> that are
equal to <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a+b+ab" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a+b+ab</annotation></semantics></math> for some choice of distinct positive integers
<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</blockquote>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The reference answer is <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{70}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn>70</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{70}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Stage 1 — Strategic Planning (<math id="A1.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>)</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The single <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;think&gt;</span> block contains no numerical computation.
It performs one algebraic restructuring of the problem—factoring
<math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a+b+ab=(a{+}1)(b{+}1)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a+b+ab=(a{+}1)(b{+}1)-1</annotation></semantics></math>—and specifies the resulting search problem
to be solved in code.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="257.25" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 257.25" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,257.25) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#1F4E79;" fill="#1F4E79" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 3.32 L 0 253.93 C 0 255.77 1.49 257.25 3.32 257.25 L 474.06 257.25 C 475.89 257.25 477.38 255.77 477.38 253.93 L 477.38 3.32 C 477.38 1.49 475.89 0 474.06 0 L 3.32 0 C 1.49 0 0 1.49 0 3.32 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F4F7FB;" fill="#F4F7FB" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.55 3.32 L 0.55 238.12 L 476.82 238.12 L 476.82 3.32 C 476.82 1.79 475.58 0.55 474.06 0.55 L 3.32 0.55 C 1.79 0.55 0.55 1.79 0.55 3.32 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 10.03 243.15)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.05em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.04em;font-size:10pt;" height="10.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="457.32"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.05em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">&lt;think&gt;</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 10.03 12.45)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:35.73em;--ltx-fo-height:15.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="218.63" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 216.21)" width="494.4"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:35.73em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">I need to find the number of integers <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 100</annotation></semantics></math> that can be written as
<math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a+b+ab" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a+b+ab</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct positive integers.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let me think about this expression: <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a+b+ab=(a{+}1)(b{+}1)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a+b+ab=(a{+}1)(b{+}1)-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">So I need to find how many integers <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 100</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy
<math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=(a{+}1)(b{+}1)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=(a{+}1)(b{+}1)-1</annotation></semantics></math> for some distinct positive integers <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b</annotation></semantics></math>.
This means <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n+1=(a{+}1)(b{+}1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n+1=(a{+}1)(b{+}1)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\neq b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≠</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\neq b</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=a{+}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=a{+}1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}=b{+}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}=b{+}1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m,n^{\prime}\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m,n^{\prime}\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\neq n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≠</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\neq n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\cdot n^{\prime}=n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\cdot n^{\prime}=n+1</annotation></semantics></math>. So I need to count how many values of <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 100</annotation></semantics></math> can
be written as <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\cdot n^{\prime}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\cdot n^{\prime}-1</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m,n^{\prime}\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m,n^{\prime}\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\neq n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≠</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\neq n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\cdot n^{\prime}\leq 101" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">101</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\cdot n^{\prime}\leq 101</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Actually, let me just brute force this. Since <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct
positive integers, let me iterate over possible values and check
which sums are <math id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 100</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="A1.SS2.p2.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Let me write code to compute this
directly.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This realises the role <span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ThinC</span> reserves for <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>
(Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 ThinC Reasoning ‣ 3 ThinC: Teaching Models to Think in Code ‣ Teaching Language Models to Think in Code" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>): a high-level strategic plan,
not a step-by-step derivation. Three properties of this think block
illustrate the design intent:</p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">No arithmetic in NL.</span> The model never evaluates an
expression or enumerates a case manually. The think channel is
used purely for symbolic restructuring of the problem.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:2.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Search-space specification.</span> It fixes the exact
constraints ( <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m,n^{\prime}\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m,n^{\prime}\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\neq n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\neq n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\cdot n^{\prime}\leq 101" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>101</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\cdot n^{\prime}\leq 101</annotation></semantics></math> )
before any code is written, providing a clean starting point for
the code blocks that follow.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:2.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Single transition to code.</span> The block ends with one
sentence (<span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">“Let me write code to compute this directly”</span>)
and from this point onward, NL does not return: every subsequent
reasoning step is carried out inside a <span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;python&gt;</span> block.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Stage 2 — Code-Centric Reasoning</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The remainder of the rollout consists of five
<span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;python&gt;</span>/<span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;result&gt;</span> exchanges. Each code block builds
on the execution outputs of the preceding blocks, as prescribed by
Eq. <a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3.1 ThinC Reasoning ‣ 3 ThinC: Teaching Models to Think in Code ‣ Teaching Language Models to Think in Code" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, and every reasoning step—including
self-correction, structural verification, and independent
re-derivation—is performed in code.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Turn 1: Initial brute force.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The model implements a direct enumeration with an early
<span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">break</span> that it pre-emptively flags as potentially incorrect.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="60.84" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 60.84" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,60.84) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#737373;" fill="#737373" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 3.32 L 0 57.52 C 0 59.35 1.49 60.84 3.32 60.84 L 474.06 60.84 C 475.89 60.84 477.38 59.35 477.38 57.52 L 477.38 3.32 C 477.38 1.49 475.89 0 474.06 0 L 3.32 0 C 1.49 0 0 1.49 0 3.32 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F8F8F4;" fill="#F8F8F4" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.55 3.32 L 0.55 25.65 L 476.82 25.65 L 476.82 3.32 C 476.82 1.79 475.58 0.55 474.06 0.55 L 3.32 0.55 C 1.79 0.55 0.55 1.79 0.55 3.32 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 7.26 30.14)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:30.41em;--ltx-fo-height:1.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="26.21" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 26.21)" width="420.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:30.41em;">
<span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">&lt;python&gt;<span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">  Turn 1</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 7.26 10.03)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.45em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.68" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="462.85"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.45em;">
<span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_language_Python ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><span class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></span>
<span id="lstnumberx1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_comment ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#6A737D;">#<span id="lstnumberx1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>(a+1)(b+1)<span id="lstnumberx1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>-<span id="lstnumberx1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>1<span id="lstnumberx1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>--<span id="lstnumberx1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>brute<span id="lstnumberx1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>force<span id="lstnumberx1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>over<span id="lstnumberx1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>distinct<span id="lstnumberx1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>(a,b)</span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">results</span><span id="lstnumberx2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">=</span><span id="lstnumberx2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_lst_keywords2 ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#8959A8;">set</span><span id="lstnumberx2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">()</span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#8959A8;">for</span><span id="lstnumberx3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">a</span><span id="lstnumberx3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#8959A8;">in</span><span id="lstnumberx3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_lst_keywords2 ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#8959A8;">range</span><span id="lstnumberx3.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(1,</span><span id="lstnumberx3.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">100):</span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">    </span><span id="lstnumberx4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#8959A8;">for</span><span id="lstnumberx4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">b</span><span id="lstnumberx4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#8959A8;">in</span><span id="lstnumberx4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_lst_keywords2 ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#8959A8;">range</span><span id="lstnumberx4.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><span id="lstnumberx4.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">a</span><span id="lstnumberx4.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">+1,</span><span id="lstnumberx4.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">100):</span><span id="lstnumberx4.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">     </span><span id="lstnumberx4.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_comment ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#6A737D;">#<span id="lstnumberx4.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>b<span id="lstnumberx4.15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>&gt;<span id="lstnumberx4.15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>a<span id="lstnumberx4.15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>to<span id="lstnumberx4.15.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>keep<span id="lstnumberx4.15.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>pairs<span id="lstnumberx4.15.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>distinct</span>
</span>
