</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Tool Call and Response Length per Benchmark</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section reports the average number of tool calls per
trajectory and the average response length on each
evaluation benchmark.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Tool Calls by Benchmark</h3>

<figure id="A3.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2605.07237v1/toolcalls_per_benchmark.svg" id="A3.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:452/249;" width="452" height="249"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Average tool calls per benchmark. We compare how often models invoke the Python interpreter across AIME 2024–2026, HMMT 2025 February, and BeyondAIME.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Response Length by Benchmark</h3>

<figure id="A3.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2605.07237v1/length_per_benchmark.svg" id="A3.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:452/249;" width="452" height="249"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Average response length per benchmark. We report the mean trajectory length across AIME 2024–2026, HMMT 2025 February, and BeyondAIME. </figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>OOD Generalization</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate <span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ThinC</span>-4B on GPQA-Diamond <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>,
a graduate-level science benchmark covering physics, chemistry,
and biology, as an out-of-distribution (OOD) test.
Table <a href="#A4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Appendix D OOD Generalization ‣ Teaching Language Models to Think in Code" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> reports avg@16 and best@16 accuracy.
<span id="A4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ThinC</span>-4B leads on both metrics, exceeding ASTER-4B by
<math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.1</annotation></semantics></math> points on avg@16 and the base model by <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7.6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7.6</annotation></semantics></math> points on
best@16, suggesting that the code-centric reasoning format
generalizes more effectively than the interleaved alternative
beyond the mathematical training domain.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>GPQA-Diamond accuracy (%). Best per column in
<span id="A4.T2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>.</figcaption>
<table id="A4.T2.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A4.T2.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T2.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Model</th>
<th id="A4.T2.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T2.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">avg@16</span></th>
<th id="A4.T2.4.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T2.4.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">best@16</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A4.T2.4.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T2.4.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Qwen3-4B-Thinking</th>
<td id="A4.T2.4.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">66.32</td>
<td id="A4.T2.4.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">83.84</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T2.4.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T2.4.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">ASTER-4B</th>
<td id="A4.T2.4.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">63.42</td>
<td id="A4.T2.4.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">90.40</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T2.4.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T2.4.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.T2.4.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ThinC</span>-4B</th>
<td id="A4.T2.4.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.T2.4.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">66.48</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.4.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.T2.4.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">91.41</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Training Details</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All training runs use a single node with <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="8\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\times</annotation></semantics></math> NVIDIA H200 GPUs.
We perform SFT using the LLaMA-Factory framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>
and RL using the verl framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>. Both
<span id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ThinC</span>-1.7B and <span id="A5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ThinC</span>-4B share identical
hyperparameter configurations at each training stage.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
